een  do you have a drop-dead date I mean is  there is there a date that you say you  know this is it we have to scuttle the  season I mean I think I know that  they're talking about that and and  that's something that I'm curious to  know what that that date is and whatever  it is Dan I just don't know how you're  you're going to get things back on track  enough to play basketball I mean really  the the first date you have to look at  is the mid-may date when the CBC comes  out presumably with new recommendations  on size of crowds if it remains at 50 or  10 even you're not doing anything in any  sport if it gets upgraded to like 500  then maybe you have yourself a ball game  there so that's a number and that's the  announcement I'm looking for next I'm  also wondering about this I talked to a  source last night and said who told me  you know what don't rule out maybe first  round three-game series and then a  five-game series and then a seven-game  series you know as you know you progress  through the playoffs could you see a  scenario where they had you know  truncated playoffs you know it's a good  question and I asked that a couple of  different ways and it's not been  discussed but it certainly is something  that I think the people I've talked to  anyway would strongly consider just to  salvage any type of postseason I mean  they look you know it did there's only a  certain amount of time they can wait  here they're not going to play games  like into September like that's just not  going to happen so if it comes to the  point where they get to July and all of  a sudden it's kind of an all-clear to  play sports maybe you try something like  that I mean it's shortened playoffs  before they used to be best of five in  the first round for a number of years so  it's not unprecedented to shorten it a  little bit and look these are these are  unique circumstances if you want to  crown a champion and have a playoffs got  to you know do things differently just  like you did in 99 with the  lockout-shortened season it was a 2011  with the next one I mean they're  desperate times if you know if you want  to to do something if you want to get  something done you have to try some  desperate measures talking to Chris  Mannix from Sports Illustrated does it  seem like it was seven and a half days  ago that Rudy  they're tested positive it feels like a  lifetime ago I mean it was its wild I  mean I just  and look I and one thing I would say and  not to criticize the NBA but there's a  lot of like NBA being the leader and all  this I mean there's guilty as everybody  else and waiting too long I mean and I  say that as a person that wrote a column  you know the day of the Rudy Gobert  stuff it said shut it down I mean this  this was an inevitability like you know  this this virus spreading onto NBA  courts and amongst NBA players and and  there's certainly an argument you made  in hindsight that you know the league  should have started down a little bit  earlier but I think man this has  happened this is all just move so fast  from you know one player testing  positive and everything getting shut  down so now we've got what as many as  seven and and I fully expect that number  to grow in the coming days and weeks to  where we are with not being able to put  ten people into a building in this  country so it's it's if it's a wild set  of circumstances the player who will be  most disappointed that this season is is  canceled would be who LeBron James  easily  I mean he's having an look where we're  putting out our si and MVP awards and  awards this year for the year today on  si.com and you know I don't know that he  would have had the NBA MVP but he had a  great chance to win a championship and  look it you know you talk about what  feels like you know a lifetime ago with  me in the passing of the tragic passing  of Kobe Bryant you know feels like so  long ago right now and you know this  would have been you know LeBrons chance  to not only win a championship another  championship but also do it in a  storybook way for the city of Los  Angeles so they I mean the way he was  playing the way the Lakers were playing  I mean coming off wins over the Bucs and  Clippers I mean it's I think he would be  the most crushed by all this good to  visit with you Chris we appreciate your  time as always I am keeping local  businesses in business Dan because I  have waffles from the same place on the  way for the sixth consecutive day in  Boston so I'm I'm ready to go have you  ever cooked for yourself  I tried okay so Paulie knows  this like I bought one of those trigger  grills in Vermont and because Paulie had  one I had to get a bigger one and I did  I got it for the outdoor deck in Vermont  officially I have cooked one hot dog on  the triggers room and you've had it for  two years  yes yes I I was over at paulie's Vermont  estate at one point and I saw him  cooking a bunch of stuff up there and I  just said I had to have one and then I  got it and first of all it took me  awhile that as an idiot to figure how to  use it and then like when I got him like  I don't really smoke things or I don't  cook a lot of things so I tossed a hot  dog and a bun on there cooked it up and  that was about I want to say nine months  ago and I haven't done anything ever  since thank you Chris  hi dad Chris Mannix Sports Illustrated

